  "gold_solution": "```python\nfrom gurobipy import *\n\ndef solve_problem():\n    m = Model(\"Transportation_Problem\")\n    m.setParam(\"TimeLimit\", 300)  # Set time limit to 300 seconds\n\n    # Data\n    sources = list(range(12))  # S0..S11\n    destinations = list(range(8))  # D0..D7\n\n    supplies = [22, 22, 21, 89, 89, 49, 88, 50, 36, 73, 100, 27]\n    demands = [64, 28, 69, 29, 58, 33, 61, 11]\n\n    # Cost matrix: rows correspond to sources S0..S11, columns to destinations D0..D7\n    costs = [\n        [ 14.05,  12.36,   5.75,  18.64,  22.85,  13.14,  28.42,   7.17],  # S0\n        [ 17.69,  11.23,  26.82,  10.94,  16.66,  26.95,  21.67,   9.45],  # S1\n        [ 12.24,  16.39,  27.50,  27.17,  23.92,  18.33,   9.62,  13.01],  # S2\n        [ 25.58,  27.95,  10.12,  11.63,  20.42,  27.87,  15.69,  21.43],  # S3\n        [ 17.62,  17.53,   8.47,  28.88,   6.17,  17.96,  11.96,  22.84],  # S4\n        [ 25.62,  15.38,  10.77,  23.35,  26.51,  22.97,   9.07,  16.24],  # S5\n        [ 21.75,   5.95,  14.68,   7.84,  15.70,   8.50,  28.77,  11.79],  # S6\n        [ 27.34,   7.02,  21.86,   9.69,  17.75,  20.24,  20.83,  13.43],  # S7\n        [  9.65,   7.57,  24.05,  14.60,  25.26,  14.63,  15.37,  14.10],  # S8\n        [  8.27,  22.31,  14.48,  27.39,  19.09,  22.89,  10.50,  27.63],  # S9\n        [ 27.59,  22.23,  11.16,  15.87,   7.98,  13.69,  12.70,  13.22],  # S10\n        [ 11.24,  28.36,  18.82,  21.92,   7.41,  28.43,  29.31,  27.18],  # S11\n    ]\n\n    # Decision variables:\n    # Flow_S{i}_D{j} >= 0 is the quantity shipped from source i to destination j\n    flows = {}\n    for i in sources:\n        for j in destinations:\n            flows[(i, j)] = m.addVar(lb=0.0, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f\"Flow_S{i}_D{j}\")\n\n    # Objective: Minimize total transportation cost\n    m.setObjective(\n        quicksum(costs[i][j] * flows[(i, j)] for i in sources for j in destinations),\n        GRB.MINIMIZE\n    )\n\n    # Supply constraints: Shipments from each source <= its supply\n    for i in sources:\n        m.addConstr(\n            quicksum(flows[(i, j)] for j in destinations) <= supplies[i],\n            name=f\"Supply_S{i}\"\n        )\n\n    # Demand constraints: Shipments to each destination >= its demand\n    for j in destinations:\n        m.addConstr(\n            quicksum(flows[(i, j)] for i in sources) >= demands[j],\n            name=f\"Demand_D{j}\"\n        )\n\n    m.optimize()\n    return m\n```",
  "LLM_description": "To: Executive Leadership and Operations\nFrom: Supply Chain Director\nDate: [Insert Date]\nSubject: Network shipping plan to meet all destination needs at the lowest total freight cost\n\nSituation\nWe operate a multi-node network of warehouses and factories supplying products to multiple stores and customers. Freight spend is a significant portion of our cost-to-serve, and lane choices directly affect both cost and on-time performance. To support reliable fulfillment and margin targets, we need a clear plan that allocates shipments across our network efficiently.\n\nProblem\nWe need to determine how much to ship from each source to each destination, recognizing that every source has limited available inventory or capacity and every destination has a firm requirement that must be fully covered. Shipping costs vary by route, so assigning destinations to the most economical sources is critical. Partial shipments are allowed, so orders can be split across multiple sources and routes; quantities do not need to be in whole pallet or truckload increments.\n\nGoal\nIdentify the most cost-effective routing plan that:\n- Meets each destination\u2019s requirement in full\n- Does not exceed available inventory or capacity at any source\n- Minimizes total shipping spend across all lanes\n\nApproach and Expected Outcome\n- Validate the supply, demand, and lane cost data.\n- Evaluate shipment allocations from each source to each destination to build a feasible plan.\n- Deliverables will include: recommended shipping quantities by lane, confirmation that all destination needs are met without over-allocating any source, estimated total freight spend, and visibility to any unused inventory. We will also highlight lanes with relatively high costs to inform future sourcing or rate negotiations.\n- After review with Operations and Transportation, we will finalize the plan for execution and monitor performance, adjusting as supply, demand, or rates change.\n\nAnnex \u2013 Shipping Data:\nDestination requirements: Store D2 needs 69 units; Store D4 needs 58 units; Store D3 needs 29 units; Store D6 needs 61 units; Store D7 needs 11 units; Store D1 needs 28 units; Store D5 needs 33 units; Store D0 needs 64 units.\n\nShipping costs by source:\n  Warehouse S0 (supply: 22 units): D7 at $7.17/unit, D5 at $13.14/unit, D2 at $5.75/unit, D6 at $28.42/unit, D3 at $18.64/unit, D1 at $12.36/unit, D4 at $22.85/unit, D0 at $14.05/unit\n  Warehouse S1 (supply: 22 units): D5 at $26.95/unit, D7 at $9.45/unit, D4 at $16.66/unit, D3 at $10.94/unit, D6 at $21.67/unit, D0 at $17.69/unit, D1 at $11.23/unit, D2 at $26.82/unit\n  Warehouse S2 (supply: 21 units): D5 at $18.33/unit, D2 at $27.50/unit, D7 at $13.01/unit, D3 at $27.17/unit, D0 at $12.24/unit, D6 at $9.62/unit, D4 at $23.92/unit, D1 at $16.39/unit\n  Warehouse S3 (supply: 89 units): D4 at $20.42/unit, D0 at $25.58/unit, D7 at $21.43/unit, D1 at $27.95/unit, D2 at $10.12/unit, D5 at $27.87/unit, D3 at $11.63/unit, D6 at $15.69/unit\n  Warehouse S4 (supply: 89 units): D3 at $28.88/unit, D1 at $17.53/unit, D2 at $8.47/unit, D5 at $17.96/unit, D0 at $17.62/unit, D4 at $6.17/unit, D7 at $22.84/unit, D6 at $11.96/unit\n  Warehouse S5 (supply: 49 units): D6 at $9.07/unit, D3 at $23.35/unit, D5 at $22.97/unit, D4 at $26.51/unit, D2 at $10.77/unit, D7 at $16.24/unit, D0 at $25.62/unit, D1 at $15.38/unit\n  Warehouse S6 (supply: 88 units): D4 at $15.70/unit, D7 at $11.79/unit, D6 at $28.77/unit, D3 at $7.84/unit, D1 at $5.95/unit, D0 at $21.75/unit, D5 at $8.50/unit, D2 at $14.68/unit\n  Warehouse S7 (supply: 50 units): D7 at $13.43/unit, D6 at $20.83/unit, D1 at $7.02/unit, D0 at $27.34/unit, D3 at $9.69/unit, D2 at $21.86/unit, D5 at $20.24/unit, D4 at $17.75/unit\n  Warehouse S8 (supply: 36 units): D1 at $7.57/unit, D2 at $24.05/unit, D6 at $15.37/unit, D4 at $25.26/unit, D7 at $14.10/unit, D0 at $9.65/unit, D5 at $14.63/unit, D3 at $14.60/unit\n  Warehouse S9 (supply: 73 units): D2 at $14.48/unit, D6 at $10.50/unit, D5 at $22.89/unit, D3 at $27.39/unit, D0 at $8.27/unit, D7 at $27.63/unit, D1 at $22.31/unit, D4 at $19.09/unit\n  Warehouse S10 (supply: 100 units): D6 at $12.70/unit, D7 at $13.22/unit, D1 at $22.23/unit, D5 at $13.69/unit, D4 at $7.98/unit, D0 at $27.59/unit, D3 at $15.87/unit, D2 at $11.16/unit\n  Warehouse S11 (supply: 27 units): D2 at $18.82/unit, D7 at $27.18/unit, D4 at $7.41/unit, D6 at $29.31/unit, D1 at $28.36/unit, D3 at $21.92/unit, D0 at $11.24/unit, D5 at $28.43/unit",
